Third-party material in this distribution
-----------------------------------------

The Rust crates satz is compiled from

    Their licence texts — one copy per crate, as the crate ships it — are in
    THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md, which travels beside this file in every release
    archive. That file is generated from Cargo.lock by cargo about
    (`scripts/update-third-party-licenses.sh`) and names every crate under the
    licence it is taken under. The entries below are the material that is not a
    crate.

Typst, and the fonts it typesets with

    `--format pdf` is typeset by Typst, compiled into this binary rather than
    called as a tool, so a PDF needs nothing installed. The engine and the eight
    font faces in assets/fonts/ travel with the binary.

    Typst: Copyright (c) The Typst Project Developers.
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
    https://github.com/typst/typst

    The font faces in assets/fonts/, taken from the `typst-assets` crate and
    compiled into this binary:

    Libertinus Serif, regular / bold / italic / bold italic — Copyright (c)
    2012-2024 The Libertinus Project Authors. Licensed under the SIL Open Font
    License, Version 1.1. https://github.com/alerque/libertinus

    DejaVu Sans Mono, regular / bold / oblique / bold oblique — Bitstream Vera
    Fonts Copyright (c) 2003 Bitstream, Inc.; the DejaVu changes are in the
    public domain. https://dejavu-fonts.github.io

    Both licences ask a redistributor to carry their text with the files, so the
    texts are beside them — assets/fonts/LICENSE-Libertinus-OFL.txt and
    assets/fonts/LICENSE-DejaVu.txt — and travel in every release archive.

